@@ -34,6 +34,8 @@ All notable, unreleased changes to this project will be documented in this file.
 
 ### GraphQL API
 
+- Added age-restricted products. Staff can set `Product.minimumAge` (1-120) through `productCreate`, `productUpdate` and `productBulkCreate`, and customers have a `User.dateOfBirth` field settable through `accountUpdate` (customer) and `customerCreate`/`customerUpdate` (staff). `checkoutCreate`, `checkoutLinesAdd`, `checkoutLinesUpdate`, `checkoutComplete` and `orderCreateFromCheckout` reject age-restricted products for guests (`AGE_RESTRICTED_LOGIN_REQUIRED`) and for customers without a date of birth or who are too young (`AGE_RESTRICTION_NOT_MET`); the failing variants are returned in the error's `variants` field. Automatic checkout completion applies the same rule.
+- The date of birth is personal data. `User.dateOfBirth` is readable only by the customer and by a super-admin looking up a single customer (`user`, `me`, `order(id:)`), never inside a list or connection and never by apps; every super-admin read and every change writes an audit `CustomerEvent` (`DATE_OF_BIRTH_READ`, `DATE_OF_BIRTH_CHANGED`) that never contains the date. Only the customer (`accountUpdate`) or a super-admin (`customerCreate`, `customerUpdate`) can set it. Other staff and apps can use the new `User.isAgeEligible(minimumAge:)` yes/no field instead. Added `Shop.timeZone` / `ShopSettingsInput.timeZone`: "today" for age checks is the current date in the shop's time zone (default `UTC`). Emails or apps that recommend products must exclude age-restricted products for customers who are not eligible; use `User.isAgeEligible(minimumAge:)`.
 - Added `deprecationReason` field to the `App` and `Manifest` types, and a new `appSelfUpdate` mutation that lets an app set it on itself. An app declares it in its manifest (`deprecationReason`) and/or sets it at any time via `appSelfUpdate`; staff users cannot set it through `appUpdate`. Pass a blank value to `appSelfUpdate` to clear it; omitting the field or passing `null` leaves it unchanged. Values longer than 2048 characters are truncated rather than rejected. A deprecated app keeps working exactly as before - the field is informational and is surfaced in the dashboard.
 - Added `identifier` field to the `Webhook` type. It holds an app-provided, stable identifier that is unique per app. It can be set through the app manifest (`webhooks[].identifier`) and the `webhookCreate`/`webhookUpdate` mutations.
 - Added `Shop.allowStorefrontTraffic` field and `ShopSettingsInput.allowStorefrontTraffic` input. When disabled, only apps and staff users may call the GraphQL API directly; anonymous requests and non-staff customers are rejected with HTTP 401 and the `STOREFRONT_TRAFFIC_NOT_ALLOWED` error code.
