+# Age-Restricted Products Addendum Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Shop-time-zone eligibility, birthday readable only by the customer and (single-lookup, audited) a super-admin, audited writes, an `isAgeEligible` flag for other staff, age labels in the storefront.
+
+**Architecture:** One new site setting (`time_zone`) feeds a lazily computed shop "today" used by the age validator, the future-date check and the flag. `User.dateOfBirth` gets a strict resolver (owner, or super-admin on a single path, never apps) that writes an audit `CustomerEvent`. Writes get the same rule plus a change event. Frontends adapt.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Django/graphene/pytest (saleor); React/TS/Apollo/jest (dashboard); Next.js/vitest (storefront).
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-20-age-restricted-products-addendum-pii-and-labels.md` (amends `2026-10-20-age-restricted-products-design.md`; the addendum wins on conflicts).
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Do NOT commit or push anywhere. Run backend commands via `docker exec saleor-benchmark-saleor-1 sh -c 'cd /app && …'`; storefront/dashboard commands from their repos (see memory note `saleor-benchmark-test-environment`).
+- Tests first, watch them fail, then implement. Follow `saleor/graphql/CLAUDE.md`: `ADDED_IN_323` on new fields, exhaustive descriptions, regenerate `saleor/graphql/schema.graphql` with `python manage.py get_graphql_schema`.
+- Never run two pytest jobs at once; add a migration, then use `--create-db` once.
+- `SiteSettings.time_zone`: IANA name, default `"UTC"`, validated with `zoneinfo`; shop "today" = `timezone.now().astimezone(ZoneInfo(tz)).date()`, computed lazily (no extra queries for carts without a restricted product).
+- `User.dateOfBirth` readable only by: the owner (never audited), or a *user* with `is_superuser` on a single-customer path (audited with `DATE_OF_BIRTH_READ`). Denied for apps, all other staff, and anywhere in a list/connection (any int or `edges` element in `info.path`).
+- `dateOfBirth` input: `customerCreate`/`customerUpdate` super-admin only; `accountUpdate` owner only (an impersonating app is refused). A real change writes `DATE_OF_BIRTH_CHANGED`. Events never contain the birthday value.
+- `User.isAgeEligible(minimumAge: Int!): Boolean!` readable by owner, super-admin, `MANAGE_USERS`, `MANAGE_STAFF`, `MANAGE_ORDERS` (users or apps); missing birthday = `false`; reads not audited.
+- Audit events are customer-centric: `user` = the customer, `parameters` = `{"actor_user_id": <staff pk>}` or `app` = the acting app.
+
+## Review Focus
