@@ -0,0 +1,85 @@
+# Age-restricted products — addendum: PII, shop time zone, labels, audit
+
+Amends `2026-10-20-age-restricted-products-design.md`. Where this addendum and the
+original disagree, this addendum wins. Everything not mentioned here is unchanged.
+
+## Requirements (from the user)
+
+1. **Visibility is not restricted, buying is.** Restricted products stay visible in lists,
+   search, product pages and cart, each with an age label such as "18+".
+2. **Marketing emails.** Saleor core sends none (verified: the notify events are all
+   transactional and there is no newsletter/campaign/recommendation code). Any email or app
+   that recommends products must not include restricted products for customers who are not
+   eligible. Core has nothing to change for this; the rule is documented (below).
+3. **Boundary and time zone.** Compare dates, not times. "Today" is the current date in the
+   *shop's* time zone. Someone eligible by birthday today is eligible today. A 29 February
+   birthday becomes eligible on 1 March in non-leap years (unchanged).
+4. **The birthday is PII.** Only the customer (own account) and a super-admin can see it.
+   It is in no public API, public profile, unauthenticated endpoint, webhook payload or
+   export. Support and sales staff cannot see it, at most a yes/no "age eligible" flag.
+   Every change and every staff read of a birthday is audit-logged.
+
+## Decisions (user approved the recommendations)
+
+- Editing the birthday needs the same rights as reading it: the customer for their own
+  account, or a super-admin. Apps never read or write it, including when impersonating.
+- The yes/no flag is `User.isAgeEligible(minimumAge: Int!): Boolean!`; a missing birthday is
+  `false`. It is readable by the customer, a super-admin, and requestors with
+  `MANAGE_USERS`, `MANAGE_STAFF` or `MANAGE_ORDERS` (users or apps). Reads of the flag are
+  not audited (it reveals no birthday).
+- Audit uses new `CustomerEvent` types: `DATE_OF_BIRTH_CHANGED` and `DATE_OF_BIRTH_READ`.
+  They record who acted and when, never the birthday value, and are visible like the other
+  customer events (`MANAGE_USERS`/`MANAGE_STAFF`).
+- To bound audit volume and bulk exposure, a super-admin can read `dateOfBirth` only on a
+  single-customer lookup (`user`, `me`, a single `order(...).user`, or the mutation payloads
+  of `customerCreate`/`customerUpdate`/`accountUpdate`). Resolving it inside any list or
+  connection (`customers`, `staffUsers`, `orders { edges { node { user }}}`, ...) is denied.
+  The customer reading their own account is never logged.
+
+## Design
+
+### Shop time zone (backend)
+- `SiteSettings.time_zone`: `CharField`, IANA name, default `"UTC"`, validated with
+  `zoneinfo`; exposed as `Shop.timeZone` and `ShopSettingsInput.timeZone`, tagged
+  `ADDED_IN_323`. One migration.
+- `get_age_restriction_violation` / `raise_if_age_restricted` take `today` from the shop time
+  zone: `timezone.now().astimezone(ZoneInfo(settings.time_zone)).date()`. The date is
+  computed lazily, only when a restricted product and a customer with a birthday are both
+  present, so ordinary carts add no queries and the exact-query-count benchmarks stay valid.
+- `User.isAgeEligible` and the future-date validation of `dateOfBirth` use the same date.
+
+### Birthday access (backend)
+- `User.dateOfBirth` resolver: allowed for the owner, or a requestor that is a *user* with
+  `is_superuser` on a single-customer path; otherwise `PermissionDenied`. Superuser reads
+  of someone else's birthday write `DATE_OF_BIRTH_READ`.
+- `dateOfBirth` input on `customerCreate`/`customerUpdate`: super-admin only (others get
+  `PermissionDenied`). On `accountUpdate`: owner only; an app impersonating a customer is
+  refused. A change writes `DATE_OF_BIRTH_CHANGED` when the stored value actually changes.
+- No change to the legacy customer webhook payload (explicit field list, no birthday). Tests
+  pin that it stays out of the payload and that an app's subscription query gets
+  `PermissionDenied`.
+- The previous behaviour (staff with `MANAGE_USERS`/`MANAGE_STAFF` and apps reading/editing)
+  is removed; its tests are replaced.
+
+### Labels (storefront)
+- Request `minimumAge` in the list, search, product page and cart documents and show an
+  `AgeLabel` ("18+") next to the product. Nothing is hidden or disabled by it.
+- Dashboard: the customer page shows the birthday field only when the API returns it (it is
+  fetched in a separate query so a `PermissionDenied` hides the field instead of breaking the
+  page). The eligibility flag is API-only: no dashboard UI for it. The dashboard product
+  list is unchanged.
+
+### Marketing rule (documentation only)
+- `CHANGELOG.md` entry stating that emails/apps recommending products must exclude restricted
+  products for ineligible customers and should use `User.isAgeEligible(minimumAge:)`.
+
+## Testing
+- Backend: shop-time-zone boundary (shop date differs from UTC date), birthday read matrix
+  (owner, super-admin single lookup, super-admin list denied, `MANAGE_USERS` denied, app
+  denied, `MANAGE_ORDERS` denied via `order.user`), write matrix (`customerUpdate`,
+  `customerCreate`, `accountUpdate`, impersonating app), audit events created for change and
+  for staff read and not for the owner's own read, event never contains the value, webhook
+  payload excludes it, `isAgeEligible` matrix, settings validation of `timeZone`.
+- Storefront: age label rendering where a pure helper exists, plus type-check/lint/tests.
+- Dashboard: field hidden when the API denies it; existing suites updated.
+- Done criteria unchanged: all gates pass locally, nothing committed.
