+# Age-restricted products — design
+
+## Goal
+
+Staff can mark a product with a minimum age. Customers who are too young cannot
+buy it. Customers have a birthday on their profile, which is the only source of
+truth for the check. Done = implemented end to end (saleor, saleor-dashboard,
+react-storefront), tests in place, everything passing locally. Nothing is
+committed (repo rule).
+
+## Decisions made with the user
+
+- Enforcement: at add-to-cart (early feedback) and at checkout completion
+  (authoritative gate).
+- Guests may browse restricted products but cannot buy them. The backend blocks
+  guest checkout containing a restricted product; the storefront asks the user
+  to sign in.
+- A customer with no birthday on file is blocked from restricted products.
+- Customers may edit their birthday after setting it (known limitation: a
+  blocked customer can change it and retry). Revisit if a "set once" rule is
+  wanted.
+- Out of scope: draft orders and staff-created orders (staff act on a
+  customer's behalf).
+
+## 1. Data model and API (saleor)
+
+- `Product.minimum_age`: nullable `PositiveSmallIntegerField`; null = unrestricted.
+  Valid range 1–120.
+- `User.date_of_birth`: nullable `DateField`; must not be in the future.
+- One migration each in `product/migrations` and `account/migrations`.
+- GraphQL:
+  - `Product.minimumAge: Int` on `ProductCreateInput` / `ProductInput` and the
+    output type.
+  - `User.dateOfBirth: Date` on `CustomerInput` (`customerCreate` /
+    `customerUpdate`), `AccountInput` (`accountUpdate`) and the output type.
+  - Additive only; no existing client breaks.
+- Permissions: existing product permissions cover `minimumAge`; customers set
+  their own birthday via `accountUpdate`; staff with `MANAGE_USERS` via
+  `customerUpdate`.
+
+## 2. Enforcement (saleor)
+
+- `validate_checkout_age_restrictions(lines, user, today)` in the checkout
+  module returns the offending lines. A line offends when its product has a
+  `minimum_age` and the buyer is a guest, has no `date_of_birth`, or is younger
+  than the minimum (computed by calendar birthday comparison, not days/365).
+- New `CheckoutErrorCode` values:
+  - `AGE_RESTRICTED_LOGIN_REQUIRED` — guest buyer.
+  - `AGE_RESTRICTION_NOT_MET` — missing birthday or too young; offending variant
+    IDs returned in the error's `variants` field.
+- Call sites:
+  - Early (lines being added): `checkoutCreate`, `checkoutLinesAdd`,
+    `checkoutLinesUpdate`.
+  - Authoritative (all lines): `checkoutComplete`, `orderCreateFromCheckout`.
+  - Not called: `checkoutCustomerAttach` / `checkoutCustomerDetach`; detaching
+    is caught at completion.
+
+## 3. Dashboard and storefront
+
+- saleor-dashboard: "Minimum age" input on the product details form; date of
+  birth field on the customer details card; update GraphQL fragments/mutations
+  and regenerate types per the repo's existing process.
+- react-storefront: birthday field on account settings; checkout maps the two
+  error codes to messages ("Sign in to buy age-restricted items" with a login
+  link; "You don't meet the age requirement for these items" naming the
+  products). Product pages remain browsable by everyone.
+
+## 4. Testing and done criteria
+
+- Backend pytest:
+  - Validator unit tests: turns 18 today, turns 18 tomorrow, leap day, guest,
+    missing birthday, mixed carts.
+  - Mutation tests for the product and customer fields: permissions and
+    validation.
+  - Checkout tests for every call site, guest and customer, including a cart
+    whose product became restricted after the line was added (completion must
+    block).
+- Frontends: component tests where the repos already have them, plus type-check
+  and lint.
+- Done: backend tests, linters and migration check pass; dashboard and
+  storefront type-check, lint and test pass; GraphQL schema file regenerated;
+  changes left uncommitted.
